---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Sporty — Terms of Service (Operational Draft)" description="Operational draft terms of service for Sporty.">
  <main class="terms-shell">
    <h1 class="section-title">Terms of Service (Operational Draft)</h1>
    <p class="lead-copy">
      These Terms are an operational draft pending legal review. They describe current service expectations and controls,
      and are not a legal certification statement.
    </p>

    <section class="terms-card">
      <h2>1. Service description and non-medical use</h2>
      <p>
        Sporty provides recommendation and forecasting tools for sports discovery. Sporty is not a medical service and does not
        provide medical diagnosis, treatment, or emergency guidance.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-card">
      <h2>2. Eligibility and account responsibility</h2>
      <p>
        You are responsible for account credentials, activity in your account, and accuracy of information you submit.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-card">
      <h2>3. Guardian responsibility for child profiles</h2>
      <p>
        Minor child usage (under 18) is only permitted through guardian-mediated flows. Guardians are responsible for attestations,
        permissions, and requests related to child profiles and child-linked processing. Child analyses require paid child credits tied to guardian card transactions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-card">
      <h2>4. Credits and billing</h2>
      <p>
        Premium analyses use credits tied to the purchasing account. Credit and payment operations are processed through
        configured payment and infrastructure providers. No free child-credit path is offered in production.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-card">
      <h2>4b. Child data handling baseline</h2>
      <p>
        Child identifiable analysis data and child results are retained for a short operational window (7 days) and then deleted under retention controls.
        Sporty does not monetize child-derived data, including child-derived aggregates, under current policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        Child data is not used in model-training or learning-event pipelines under current policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        No retention-extension option is offered at launch; guardians should use the child-results PDF export if they need records beyond the 7-day window.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-card">
      <h2>5. Refund policy</h2>
      <p>
        Default rule: no refunds for credits or completed services.
      </p>
      <p>
        Exception: where applicable law, card-network rules, or payment-provider requirements mandate a refund or equivalent remedy,
        those requirements apply.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-card">
      <h2>6. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        You agree not to misuse the service, bypass controls, interfere with security, or use the product for unlawful activity.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-card">
      <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        Sporty product content, code, and branding remain owned by Sporty and licensors. You receive a limited right to use the
        service under these Terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-card">
      <h2>8. Warranty and liability limitations (draft)</h2>
      <p>
        The service is provided on an "as available" basis. To the extent permitted by applicable law, Sporty disclaims implied
        warranties and limits liability for indirect or consequential losses.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-card">
      <h2>9. Governing law and venue (EU default draft)</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are intended to follow EU-default governing law and venue posture aligned with Sporty’s EU registration.
        Final jurisdiction and venue text remains pending legal finalization.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-card">
      <h2>10. Changes to these Terms</h2>
      <p>
        Sporty may update these Terms as the product and legal requirements evolve. Material updates will be published with an
        updated effective date and reasonable notice mechanism.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-card">
      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Legal contact: TODO</li>
        <li>Privacy contact: TODO</li>
        <li>Security incident contact: TODO</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="lead-copy">Operational draft; legal review pending.</p>
  </main>

  <Fragment slot="scripts">
    <script is:inline src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@supabase/supabase-js@2" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="/config.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="/assets/js/app.js?v=8" defer></script>
  </Fragment>
</BaseLayout>
